Third-party material
- theme/vendor/whitesur-kvantum: WhiteSur Kvantum theme by vinceliuice, GPL-3.0
  (https://github.com/vinceliuice/WhiteSur-kde). Recolored at build time.
- install/cursors/Bibata-Modern-Ice.tar.xz: the Bibata cursor theme by ful1e5,
  GPL-3.0 (https://github.com/ful1e5/Bibata_Cursor), v2.0.7 bundled verbatim;
  install.sh extracts it into ~/.local/share/icons.
- The Plasma desktop theme starts from KDE's Breeze "default" theme installed on the system
  (LGPL-2.0-or-later); only its SVG fills are changed and the frames are redrawn.
- system/gestures/install-gestures.sh downloads libinput-gestures by Mark Blakeney (GPL-3.0) at install time;
  it is not part of this repository.
- plasmoids/org.aether.ribbons/contents/ui/logos.js: distribution logos from Simple Icons
  (CC0-1.0, https://simpleicons.org); each logo is its project's trademark.
- Fonts (Inter by Rasmus Andersson, SIL OFL-1.1, https://github.com/rsms/inter;
  JetBrainsMono Nerd Font — JetBrains Mono by JetBrains, SIL OFL-1.1,
  https://www.jetbrains.com/lp/mono/, with the Nerd Fonts patches,
  https://www.nerdfonts.com) and icon themes (Papirus) are not bundled;
  install/fonts.sh fetches the fonts at install time, Papirus comes from your
  distribution.
- The lens segmenter, when enabled, runs Ultralytics YOLO (AGPL-3.0,
  https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics; brings PyTorch and OpenCV) as a
  separate local process — it is a user-installed optional dependency, never
  linked or bundled here — and the MobileSAM weights (Apache-2.0,
  https://github.com/ChaoningZhang/MobileSAM) downloaded from Ultralytics'
  asset releases (https://github.com/ultralytics/assets). OCR runs tesseract
  (Apache-2.0) from your distribution.
